  message: "Closed by Phase 6 PR2 (commit 98533c0fff). metrics.compute_metrics canonical: total_files = unique_paths_in_analysis = len({n.path for n in nodes if n.path}). Profile-language sum moved to debug.profile_files_sum for introspection. Self-analysis: total_files=915 matches unique_paths_in_analysis (was 1217 vs 915, gap of 296). Needs bakeoff validation."  # 9c88
- op: discuss  # 728b
  at: '2026-06-02T03:37:31Z'  # 728b
  by: agent  # 728b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 728b
  clock: 7  # 728b
  nonce: 728b  # 728b
  message: "Pass-22 confirmation observation — file-accounting gap still present.\n\nPass-22 substrate measures three different file counts in adjacent fields of `metrics.debug`:\n- metrics.debug.analyzed_file_symbols = 901\n- metrics.debug.unique_paths_in_analysis = 915\n- metrics.debug.profile_files_sum = 1217\n- metrics.total_files = 915\n\nThree of these (901, 915, 1217) disagree. Pass-20 INV-mozaf reported the same structural disagreement with different numbers (902 vs 1198). The disagreement persists; only the magnitudes shifted (likely because the substrate is now post-INV-sugat-closure with the new analyzer outputs).\n\nINV-mozaf is currently `pending_validation`; suggest flip pending_validation → violated.\n\nLab notebook entry: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06012026_2340_pass22.md`."  # 728b
- op: discuss  # 9a9c
  at: '2026-06-02T05:28:04Z'  # 9a9c
  by: agent  # 9a9c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9a9c
  clock: 8  # 9a9c
  nonce: 9a9c  # 9a9c
  message: "Pass-25 cross-format consistency probe — file-accounting gap reproduces at one more pair:\n\nF25.3: profile.languages.python.files = 851 vs file-kind nodes with language='python' = 844. Delta = 7 files reported by profile.languages but absent from file-nodes. limits.failed_files = []; limits.truncated_files = []; limits.skipped_languages = []. The 7 are not failure-marked anywhere. Likely cause: files scanned by the file walker but skipped at AST stage (empty `__init__.py`, parse errors silently dropped, or excluded by .gitignore rules consumed after walker but before analyzer).\n\nSame shape as INV-mozaf's existing finding (metrics.total_files=1198 vs unique_paths_in_analysis=902 vs distinct non-external paths in nodes=901). Pass-25 adds a per-language angle: profile.languages.python.files (851) and file-kind nodes with language='python' (844) should be the same set; they differ by 7. The statement could extend from \"metrics.total_files equals the number of files that contributed at least one node\" to \"per-language profile.languages.<lang>.files equals count of file-kind nodes with language=<lang>\" — the same invariant at finer granularity.\n\nPass-25 also separately confirmed (NULL finding): metrics.total_nodes=34253 matches len(nodes)=34253 exactly; metrics.total_edges=109915 matches len(edges)=109915 exactly; metrics.avg_confidence=0.8 matches computed mean(edge.confidence)=0.799786. So the top-level aggregate counters are correct; the gap is specifically in the file-count axis where two surfaces (filesystem walker vs AST emitter) report differently."  # 9a9c
